README:340 [PREFIX] run
   README: Run Maestro flows against a simulator or emulator. No visual regression: reports step pass/fail and captures a screenshot on failure (see --keep-alive, --logs, --flow)
   help:   Run Maestro flows against a simulator or emulator. No visual regression — reports step pass/fail and captures a screenshot on failure.
README:341 [EXACT] record
   README: Record a simulator or emulator and extract PNG frames at exact requested timestamps
   help:   Record a simulator or emulator and extract PNG frames at exact requested timestamps.
README:342 [PREFIX] hierarchy
   README: Dump the UI hierarchy of a booted simulator or emulator without relaunching the app (reads a `run --keep-alive` session)
   help:   Dump the UI hierarchy of a booted simulator or emulator without relaunching the app.
README:343 [PREFIX] build build
   README: Build the app for a simulator (xcodebuild) or emulator (Gradle); `grantiva build` alone runs this
   help:   Build the app for a simulator (xcodebuild) or emulator (Gradle).
README:344 [PREFIX] build install
   README: Build and install the app on a simulator or emulator, then optionally launch it (--no-launch to skip)
   help:   Build and install the app on a simulator or emulator, then optionally launch it.
README:345 [EXACT] ci run
   README: Run full CI pipeline: capture screenshots, compare against baselines, upload results
   help:   Run full CI pipeline: capture screenshots, compare against baselines, upload results.
README:346 [EXACT] diff capture
   README: Navigate to configured screens and capture screenshots
   help:   Navigate to configured screens and capture screenshots.
README:347 [EXACT] diff compare
   README: Diff current captures against baselines
   help:   Diff current captures against baselines.
README:348 [EXACT] diff approve
   README: Promote current captures to baselines
   help:   Promote current captures to baselines.
README:349 [DIFF] simulator ensure
   README: Create or reuse a named simulator and boot it (--name alone reuses an existing one)
   help:   Create or reuse a named simulator and boot it. `--name` alone reuses an existing simulator with that name. To create one, the name must contain a device model ("iPhone 17") or --device-type must be given; the newest installed runtime is used unless --runtime is passed.
README:350 [EXACT] simulator delete
   README: Explicitly delete a named simulator
   help:   Explicitly delete a named simulator.
351 UNPARSED grantiva simulator sessions List Grantiva-managed simulator capacity slots
352 UNPARSED grantiva simulator teardown End a managed session, or reclaim one simulator by UDID when no ledger entry exists (--udid <UDID> --force)
README:353 [EXACT] simulator cleanup
   README: Delete Grantiva-created simulators that are shut down and not part of an active session
   help:   Delete Grantiva-created simulators that are shut down and not part of an active session.
README:354 [EXACT] emulator ensure
   README: Create the AVD when missing (installing its system image first) and boot it; stdout is the serial, or with --no-boot the AVD name (the serial when it is already running)
   help:   Create the AVD when missing (installing its system image first) and boot it. stdout is the serial, or with --no-boot the AVD name (the serial when it is already running).
README:355 [EXACT] emulator delete
   README: Delete an AVD Grantiva created; others need --force; a running AVD is never deleted
   help:   Delete an AVD Grantiva created. Others need --force. A running AVD is never deleted.
README:356 [EXACT] emulator sessions
   README: List the emulators Grantiva started
   help:   List the emulators Grantiva started.
README:357 [PREFIX] emulator teardown
   README: Kill emulators Grantiva started: one by --serial, or --all
   help:   Kill emulators Grantiva started: one by serial, or all of them. Stops the UIAutomator2 server and removes the serial's adb forwards first.
README:358 [PREFIX] console
   README: Manage your Grantiva dashboard from the terminal (see `grantiva console --help`)
   help:   Manage your Grantiva dashboard from the terminal.
README:359 [EXACT] auth login
   README: Authenticate with Grantiva API
   help:   Authenticate with Grantiva API.
README:360 [EXACT] auth status
   README: Show current authentication status
   help:   Show current authentication status.
README:361 [EXACT] auth logout
   README: Remove saved authentication credentials
   help:   Remove saved authentication credentials.
README:362 [PREFIX] doctor
   README: Check environment and dependencies (non-zero exit if a required check fails)
   help:   Check environment and dependencies.
README:363 [EXACT] runner install
   README: Extract or update the embedded runner binary
   help:   Extract or update the embedded runner binary.
README:364 [EXACT] runner version
   README: Show the embedded runner version
   help:   Show the embedded runner version.
README:365 [EXACT] runner start
   README: Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android) and keep it alive for interactive use
   help:   Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android) and keep it alive for interactive use.
README:366 [EXACT] runner stop
   README: Stop the running runner session
   help:   Stop the running runner session.
README:367 [EXACT] runner dump-hierarchy
   README: Dump the view hierarchy from a running app for agent inspection
   help:   Dump the view hierarchy from a running app for agent inspection.
README:368 [PREFIX] mcp
   README: Start the Grantiva MCP server for AI agent integration (tool list: docs/mcp.md)
   help:   Start the Grantiva MCP server for AI agent integration.
README:369 [EXACT] init
   README: Generate grantiva.yml (iOS) or grantiva-android.yml (Android) in the current directory
   help:   Generate grantiva.yml (iOS) or grantiva-android.yml (Android) in the current directory.
LEAVES NOT LISTED (excluding console subgroups): ['simulator_sessions', 'simulator_teardown']
